course: dictionary
lesson: 11925
title: Calibrated: checked to be exactly right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Calibrated means checked and adjusted so that something measures exactly right. «Before the test, Mrs Patel calibrated the scales so they read zero when empty.» Scales that are not calibrated can give wrong numbers, so the check matters. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Checked and adjusted fits well, so that is the meaning.
explain: Calibrated can also mean marked with a scale of numbers for measuring. «The jug is calibrated in millilitres, so you can read exactly how much water you pour.» The lines and numbers on the side are the clue. Look at the words around the word, and at the picture or object if you have one.
explain: The word can describe more than machines. «The speaker gave a carefully calibrated answer that pleased everyone.» Here calibrated means carefully planned or adjusted for a purpose. Try your meaning in the sentence: a carefully adjusted answer still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Calibrated means checked and adjusted so that it measures exactly right.
fact: «Calibrated» is the past form of the verb calibrate, which means to check and adjust a measuring tool.
fact: Before an experiment, you check that a balance reads 0 when it is empty, because a calibrated balance gives correct results.
fact: Calibrated can also mean marked with a scale of numbers for measuring, as in «a calibrated cylinder».
fact: A calibrated oven or tyre gauge gives correct numbers, and a carefully calibrated answer is one that has been planned for a purpose.
exercise: «The balance was calibrated so it read 0 when empty.» What does calibrated mean here? | Painted a bright colour | Filled with water | Broken and thrown away | *Checked and adjusted so it measures exactly right
exercise: «The measuring jug is calibrated in millilitres.» What does calibrated show here? | It is very heavy | *It has a scale of numbers for measuring | It can talk | It is made of glass only
exercise: Ravi says calibrated means a rough guess. Which is correct? | *Checked so that it is accurate, not guessed | A rough guess | Lost for ever | Broken
test: «A calibrated oven gives the correct temperature.» What does this tell you? | *The oven has been checked and adjusted to be accurate | The oven cannot be turned on | The oven is a new colour | The oven is always too hot
test: «The speaker gave a carefully calibrated answer.» Which word is closest in meaning to calibrated here? | Silly | Noisy | Rushed | *Carefully planned
exam: «The tyre gauge was calibrated, so the number it showed was right.» Which explains calibrated best? | Covered in mud | Very old and rusty | *Checked and adjusted to give correct readings | Bigger than the wheel
